  "Question": "Use the school flagpole as the origin, due east as the positive x-direction, and due north as the positive y-direction, with 1 unit representing 10 m. The cafeteria has coordinates \\((3,-4)\\), and the dormitory has coordinates \\((3,2)\\). How many meters apart are they? (Unit: m.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "60",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The two points have the same x-coordinate, so the segment joining them is parallel to the y-axis. The distance is \\(|2-(-4)|=6\\) units, or \\(6\\times10=60\\text{ m}\\).",
